.TH LIBINPUT 1 "July 2026" "libinput 1.31.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
libinput \- inspect Linux input devices and events
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B libinput
[\fB--help\fR|\fB--version\fR] \fIcommand\fR [\fIarguments\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B libinput
is the command dispatcher supplied by libinput-rs.  Its built-in diagnostic
commands read evdev directly, so they remain useful while diagnosing the
shared library or compositor integration.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list-devices
List readable kernel input devices and their capabilities.
.TP
.B debug-events
Print raw kernel input events.  Use
.B --device /dev/input/eventX
to restrict the stream to one device.
.TP
.B elan-recover
Reinitialize an ELAN I2C controller that remains present but has stopped
reporting events.  This command accepts
.B --device I2C-ID
or discovers all devices currently bound to
.BR elan_i2c .
It requires root privileges and refuses every other kernel driver.  The
.B --affected-only
option exits without changing hardware unless the system is an affected
ThinkPad P53.
.PP
Other command names are dispatched to matching
.B /usr/libexec/libinput/libinput-COMMAND
helpers when installed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --help
Show command help.
.TP
.B --version
Show the compatible libinput version and implementation name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libinput-rs (8),
.BR libinput (4)
